<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclude filter.

  Intentionally near-empty for now. `sh.tamga.sdk.crypto` (native Ed25519,
  AES-GCM, HKDF, ECDSA, and RSA verification; see CLAUDE.md's "Crypto
  Architecture") is the one package where SpotBugs' static analysis is most
  likely to produce noise that isn't actually wrong: add a narrowly-scoped
  Match exclusion there if/when a specific rule proves to be a false
  positive against that package's real design, with a comment explaining
  WHY it's a false positive. Do not add a blanket package-wide exclusion for
  `crypto` preemptively: that package is exactly where security-reviewer
  mandates the tightest scrutiny, and SpotBugs findings there are signal,
  not noise, until proven otherwise.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <!--
    TamgaJsonMapper.instance() intentionally returns the shared, module-wide
    ObjectMapper instance rather than a defensive copy. Jackson's own docs
    recommend reusing a single configured ObjectMapper: it is thread-safe
    for concurrent reads once configured, and construction/configuration is
    comparatively expensive, so copying it on every call would defeat the
    entire point of sharing it, for a mutation risk this codebase's own
    call sites never exercise (nothing here calls a mutating method on the
    returned mapper). A false positive against this specific, deliberate
    design, not a case to fix.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="sh.tamga.sdk.model.TamgaJsonMapper" />
    <Method name="instance" />
    <Bug pattern="MS_EXPOSE_REP" />
  </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
